thiolus saith, it serves all the uses for which Cypress, or the East Privet, is appointed by Dioscorides and Galen. He further saith, That the oil that is made of the flowers of Privet infused therein, and set in the Sun, is singularly good for the inflammations of wounds, and for the headache, coming of a hot cause. There is a sweet water also distilled from the flowers, that is good for all those diseases that need cooling and drying, and therefore helps all fluxes of the belly or stomach, bloody-fluxes, and women’s courses, being either drank or applied; as all those that void blood at the mouth, or any other place, and for distillations of rheum in the eyes, especially if it be used with them.","spans":[{"start":108,"end":113,"concept_id":"skin_ulcers","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":118,"end":129,"concept_id":"mouth_gums","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":143,"end":156,"concept_id":"inflammation","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":433,"end":446,"concept_id":"inflammation","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":450,"end":456,"concept_id":"wounds","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":470,"end":478,"concept_id":"headache","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":649,"end":668,"concept_id":"diarrhea","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":681,"end":694,"concept_id":"dysentery","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":819,"end":853,"concept_id":"conjunctivitis","polarity":"therapeutic"}]}},"images":[]}